============================================================
  BUS PASS TABLES - DIAGRAM INSTRUCTIONS
  File: bus_pass_tables.drawio
  Project: Bus Pass System | SQL Training
============================================================

NOTE: This file describes the Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD)
      for the bus_pass database. The actual .drawio diagram must
      be created manually in draw.io (app.diagrams.net).

INSTRUCTIONS TO CREATE THE DIAGRAM:
  1. Open your browser and go to: https://app.diagrams.net/
  2. Choose "Create New Diagram" → Select "Entity Relationship" template.
  3. Draw the following three tables with their columns and relationships.
  4. Save the file as: bus_pass_tables.drawio
  5. Export a PNG screenshot and save as: bus_pass_tables.png

------------------------------------------------------------
TABLE STRUCTURE TO DRAW:
------------------------------------------------------------

[passengers]
  PK  passenger_id    INT AUTO_INCREMENT
      full_name       VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
      roll_number     VARCHAR(20)  UNIQUE NOT NULL
      class           VARCHAR(10)  NOT NULL
      section         CHAR(1)
      contact_number  CHAR(10)
      address         TEXT
      created_at      TIMESTAMP

[routes]
  PK  route_id        INT AUTO_INCREMENT
      route_name      VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
      start_point     VARCHAR(100)
      end_point       VARCHAR(100)
      distance_km     DECIMAL(5,2)
      monthly_fee     DECIMAL(8,2) NOT NULL

[bus_passes]
  PK  pass_id         INT AUTO_INCREMENT
  FK  passenger_id    INT  → passengers.passenger_id
  FK  route_id        INT  → routes.route_id
      pass_number     VARCHAR(20) UNIQUE NOT NULL
      issue_date      DATE NOT NULL
      expiry_date     DATE NOT NULL
      is_active       BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE
      fee_paid        DECIMAL(8,2) NOT NULL

------------------------------------------------------------
RELATIONSHIPS:
------------------------------------------------------------
  passengers  (1) ────── (M)  bus_passes    [One passenger → many passes over time]
  routes      (1) ────── (M)  bus_passes    [One route → many passes issued]

RELATIONSHIP TYPE: One-to-Many (both relationships)

------------------------------------------------------------
DIAGRAM TIPS IN DRAW.IO:
------------------------------------------------------------
  - Use the ERD shape library (Extras → Edit Diagram or search "ERD")
  - Use crow's foot notation for 1-to-many relationships
  - Colour: passengers = Blue, routes = Green, bus_passes = Orange
  - Draw arrows from FK in bus_passes to PK in referenced tables
  - Add a title: "Bus Pass System - ERD"

============================================================
